# Interview Questions

### What is an Array?

An array is a collection of elements of the same data type stored in continuous memory locations.

### Why do we use Arrays?

Arrays reduce the number of variables and allow easy access to data using indexes.

### Difference between Variable and Array

A variable stores one value.

An array stores multiple values of the same data type.

### What is Array Indexing?

Array indexing is used to access elements of an array.

The first index always starts from **0**.

### What happens if we access outside the array?

It leads to **Undefined Behaviour**.

It may produce a garbage value, crash the program, or corrupt memory.

